// A path that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error for open
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Paths). Mode "w" is the dangerous one: a consumer that
// truncates the String creates and truncates the shorter file, then reports
// that it opened the path the program named.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: path open
print "before";
var f = open("/tmp/loxpp_probe_nul_open" + chr(0) + "tail", "w");
print "opened";
